From ff0f5383aac9a984363eef5992b329fa246e93fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: batch-validate solicited/high-bandwidth SHORTTX and
 coalesce incoming TX bursts

Validate incoming SHORTTX reconciliation responses and coalesced P2P TX bursts
via ProcessTxBatch to amortize cs_main and parallel script verification.

Original-Commit: d829b38babf16b689331c1679c1560f2b34aa05e
Original-Patch: ecash/031
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Complete actual incoming burst batching with ProcessSingleTx/ProcessTxBatch definitions relocated from31 and preserve the full original 301-line proactive-push/fallback fixture. Pending-request APIs, single known-tx method, timing constants and bad-signature request setup already reside in complete earlier owners; omit duplicates. Endpoint classification will verify the separately relocated HandleShortTx batch-consumer upgrade remains present.
